  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CELAM:  Integrated Programme on Human Rights, Peace-building and Democracy</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To provide overall leadership and coordination for the Church throughout Latin America and the Caribbean to guide and strengthen its work for social justice and development

To promote an ongoing reflection among Church leaders and pastoral workers based on Catholic Social Teaching in order to develop strategies and actions that respond to the present social, economic, political and environmental challenges facing the region.

To train Church leaders and pastoral agents throughout Latin America on the Church&#x2019;s option for the poor in the context of increasing marginalisation and poverty, human rights violations, violence and conflict, migration, environmental justice, 

To provide tools and training  to enable Church leader and committed lay people to speak out with authority on issues of labour rights, economic justice, peace-building and environmental and social protection.</narrative>
  </description>
